@* Styles of the billing screens (rendered once by each page; the back office has no CSS isolation bundle). Text keeps a
   contrast of at least 4.5:1; a status is shown by its text and its icon, never by its colour alone. Logical properties
   for the future right-to-left layout. *@
<style>
    .billing-facts { display: grid; grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr; gap: 0.25rem 1rem; margin: 0; }
    .billing-facts dt { color: #4a5361; font-size: 0.875rem; }
    .billing-facts dd { margin: 0; }
    .billing-number { text-align: end; white-space: nowrap; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
    .billing-totals { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr max-content; gap: 0.125rem 1.5rem; max-inline-size: 26rem; margin-inline-start: auto; }
    .billing-totals dt { margin: 0; }
    .billing-totals dd { margin: 0; text-align: end; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
    .billing-totals .billing-total { font-weight: 700; border-block-start: 1px solid #1b1f24; padding-block-start: 0.25rem; }
    .billing-muted { color: #4a5361; }
    .billing-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
    .billing-scroll:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #0b57d0; outline-offset: 2px; }
    .billing-mentions p { margin: 0 0 0.375rem; }
</style>
